          "text": "{\"edits\":[{\"path\":\"/scenes/2/variants/2/text\",\"value_json\":\"Mina inspected the post and discovered a crowded row of hooks, with hardly any room between two old sun hats. “There you are,” she whispered, choosing a snug place among them.\"},{\"path\":\"/scenes/6/variants/0/text\",\"value_json\":\"With the post’s crowded hooks in mind, Mina chose a snug perch among them for the ribboned invitations.\"},{\"path\":\"/endings/4/text\",\"value_json\":\"The invitation rested on the high hook, its ribbon fluttering like a tiny flag. Pip’s paper sail had carried it safely, Mina rang the rooftop bell, and a neighbor waved from beyond the chimney. Pip sneezed a silver star.\"}]}",
